blurb = "Depicts a moonlit scene of Harajuku Yoemon in a chequered robe attacking a person labeled as \"villain\" against the backgrop of pine trees. The location is the Hara station of the Tōkaidō, in present-day Shizuoka prefecture.

One source claims that this was a private commission by the prominent Uematsu family, descendants of this Yoemon, who may have in reality been a bandit. The inscription at the top reads:

[i]Yoemon was a farmer from Harajuku. By nature gentle and compassionate, he stood up to the powerful and aided the weak, coming to own numerous estates. Though his family prospered, he remained humble and unpretentious, showing kindness to the poor and diligently tending to his work. One night, while walking, he came upon a traveler being harassed by criminals and intervened. His acts of courage and righteousness are too numerous to count. His descendants continue to prosper to this day.[/i]"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
